From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wings Build <wings@example.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 02:35:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] cccs: increase update-firmware command timeouts

On NAND/TrustFence systems, update-firmware may need several seconds to
query the active system and update the redundant U-Boot environment.
CCCS runs these commands synchronously during on-the-fly SWU processing
and previously allowed only two seconds, causing DRM to reject downloads
or report a failed update even when the same command completed
successfully from the shell.

Increase only these update-firmware command timeouts to 30 seconds.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [product-specific timeout for NAND/TrustFence]

---
 library/src/cc_firmware_update.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/library/src/cc_firmware_update.c b/library/src/cc_firmware_update.c
--- a/library/src/cc_firmware_update.c
+++ b/library/src/cc_firmware_update.c
@@ -1182 +1182 @@ static int firmware_on_the_fly(const unsigned int target)
-		if (ldx_process_execute_cmd("update-firmware -a -s", &resp, 2) != 0 || resp == NULL) {
+		if (ldx_process_execute_cmd("update-firmware -a -s", &resp, 30) != 0 || resp == NULL) {
@@ -1470 +1470 @@ static void firmware_reset_cb(unsigned int const target, ccapi_bool_t *system_reset
-		if (ldx_process_execute_cmd("update-firmware --swap-active-system --no-reboot", &resp, 2) != 0) {
+		if (ldx_process_execute_cmd("update-firmware --swap-active-system --no-reboot", &resp, 30) != 0) {
-- 
2.34.1
